---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Live Scoring Privacy Policy"
	description="Privacy Policy for Live Scoring, the free two-team scoreboard app for iOS, Android and the web"
	pubDate={new Date('November 1 2026')}
>
	<h2>Privacy Policy for Live Scoring</h2>
	<p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> November 1, 2026</p>

	<h3>Overview</h3>
	<p>
		Live Scoring by netmetrics.cloud ("we", "our", or "us") is a simple scorekeeping application
		for iOS, Android, and the web. We do not ask for your name, email address, or any account,
		and we never sell data. This policy describes the small amount of data the app does handle
		and how you can control it.
	</p>

	<h3>Game Data</h3>
	<p>
		Scores, team names, team colors, and game history are stored locally on your device (or in
		your browser's local storage on the web). This data stays on your device unless you choose
		to share results or turn on live streaming. You can delete all of it at any time from
		<strong>Advanced &gt; Clear Storage</strong> inside the app.
	</p>

	<h3>Live Streaming (Optional)</h3>
	<p>
		If you turn on live streaming, the current score, team names, and team colors are sent to
		our servers (Google Firebase) under a random 6-character stream code so that anyone with the
		code or link can watch the game. No information about you or your device is included.
		Stream data expires automatically a few hours after the last update, and turning streaming
		off marks the stream inactive immediately.
	</p>

	<h3>Usage Analytics</h3>
	<p>
		The app uses Google Analytics for Firebase to understand how it is used so we can improve
		it. This records anonymous events such as "game started" or "results shared", along with
		general information like app version, device model, operating system, language, and
		country-level location derived from your network address. Events are tied to a random
		analytics ID generated for this installation, not to your name or any account. Scores, team
		names, and stream codes are never sent to analytics.
	</p>
	<p>
		You can turn analytics off at any time in <strong>Advanced &gt; Usage analytics</strong>.
		Doing so stops collection and deletes the analytics ID for this device. The app does not
		request permission to track you across other apps or websites, and does not use advertising
		identifiers.
	</p>

	<h3>Feature Settings</h3>
	<p>
		On startup the app downloads a small configuration file from Firebase Remote Config that
		turns optional features (such as SharePlay on iOS) on or off. This request does not include
		any personal information.
	</p>

	<h3>SharePlay (iOS)</h3>
	<p>
		When available, SharePlay lets people on a FaceTime call see the score together. Score
		updates travel through Apple's SharePlay service and are not stored by us.
	</p>

	<h3>Third-Party Services</h3>
	<p>
		The services above are provided by Google (Firebase) and, for SharePlay, Apple. Their
		handling of data is governed by their own privacy policies:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">Firebase Privacy and Security</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy Policy</a></li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not use advertising networks and we do not share or sell your data to anyone else.
	</p>

	<h3>Cookies</h3>
	<p>
		The web version uses browser local storage to save your game data and preferences, and
		Google Analytics may store a first-party cookie or local storage entry holding the random
		analytics ID. No advertising or cross-site tracking cookies are used.
	</p>

	<h3>Children's Privacy</h3>
	<p>
		This app is suitable for users of all ages. We do not knowingly collect personal information
		from anyone, including children, and the analytics described above is anonymous.
	</p>

	<h3>App Store Information</h3>
	<p>
		When you download Live Scoring from the App Store or Google Play, Apple or Google may
		collect information according to their own privacy policies. We do not receive personally
		identifiable information from them beyond aggregated, anonymous download and crash
		statistics that they provide to all developers.
	</p>

	<h3>Changes to This Policy</h3>
	<p>
		We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this
		page and inside the app with an updated "Last Updated" date.
	</p>

	<h3>Contact Us</h3>
	<p>
		If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:
	</p>
	<p>
		<a href="mailto:support@netmetrics.cloud">support@netmetrics.cloud</a>
	</p>
</Layout>
